[{"id":"VRCE-1-69-1","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":69,"verse":1,"english":"Then next morning Janaka skilled in speech, having in company with the Maharsis performed his daily duties, addressed the priest Satānanda, saying","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-70-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1069001","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c6e7b135af668888f5a32d25e581a32c137b385f62563e5f0f78d5bb6754ddb1","compact":"d799cd5cdb68a3608f5a35a737a7a1fe8e125409df780032ad95d81123f26313","nasal":"427bfda462d01348679e8d7077471c0889e698c41131f990d1f241a2d8839b48"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-69-2","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":69,"verse":2,"english":"My highly energetic, puissant and eminently righteous brother known by the name of Kusadhvaja dwell in the auspicious city, Sāņkāśyā, whose ramparts are ranged round with pointed weapons, and which is laved by the river Ikşumatī, and which resembles the celestial regions or the aerial car, Pușpaka.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.81,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-70-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1069002","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4c92b683bf6fc01e22b764a3e409306abafc81bbc3321a23eee11ba9ae1ebf36","compact":"2f7ba791e36cd22ee7cd2c7368166ca8344524c3f4fec2bf8d0deec43509cf02","nasal":"2f7ba791e36cd22ee7cd2c7368166ca8344524c3f4fec2bf8d0deec43509cf02"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-69-3","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":69,"verse":3,"english":"My highly energetic, puissant and eminently righteous brother known by the name of Kusadhvaja dwell in the auspicious city, Sāņkāśyā, whose ramparts are ranged round with pointed weapons, and which is laved by the river Ikşumatī, and which resembles the celestial regions or the aerial car, Pușpaka.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.884,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-70-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1069003","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c5977785273cdcdf8ad6a91d846e3f369d5d70817b6900447adefea51765feb9","compact":"dcb018e0329d4118aab30a3ad478a49074b2557978bf1bd207199f1141323bd3","nasal":"fb9eeda8c798bbcd9b54852a8e649f6c5be450231c3c944eced309c87c5e084a"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-69-4","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":69,"verse":4,"english":"I wish to see him, and he is in charge of my sacrifice. And that highly energetic one will partake with me the joy of this occasion.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-70-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1069004","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"92de5e70ad458b3832df8d11f16624bb610c9c0f9bd55a28995deae45b7034d5","compact":"257ffb8a98488939f48dd87db3f3d89d877ccb58b07642cc3ad39a81da5e74af","nasal":"257ffb8a98488939f48dd87db3f3d89d877ccb58b07642cc3ad39a81da5e74af"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-69-5","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":69,"verse":5,"english":"And commanded by the monarch, off they want, mounting on fleet coursers, with the view of bringing over that tiger among men, like Viş nu at the mandate of Indra.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-70-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1069005","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"30b12de06b62e34cf26a63c1ab04334d6134285ff49009b69b215cba9b03f2c7","compact":"2667a4e4173da5067acb60831dcb2cafcfe36bb753cba6c2bc3918a87c8c7554","nasal":"5595ba276b9dc4969be4a9aaef778e428820352e1ad49bc14b274a27670b2456"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-69-6","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":69,"verse":6,"english":"And hearing the tidings conveyed by those foremost of envoys endowed with great fleetness, Kusadhvaja set out at the mandate of the monarch.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-70-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1069006","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2607a6ca5e488521776a7203b30dbf23bd987833c33ac931bc51bc69ea35ecb7","compact":"345ecb963fae35123535b677302a6ef5d7500b003d9f3e4ba1188ffae0933c4c","nasal":"d3582e8539c9d8e9656ff64c94d93b4612bc099b8def47812c546a1b310346e4"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-69-7","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":69,"verse":7,"english":"And on coming to Videha, he appeared before the high-souled Janaka addicted to righteousness. And saluting Satānanda as well as the eminently virtuous Janaka, he sat down on an excellent and superb seat worthy of a King.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.729,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-70-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1069007","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9d5c1f60f0d3c967bfe5ac88791cc0836be4061d2aa0ea1028431ff6b01aeca2","compact":"6af8770801b946574d9b1f243c24c071ec48d6075d71c747892ded8e4b9d72ac","nasal":"91d2428f45abdcc1b51c728ac13ea914f451f89d1d5926be6a8e94595576d63f"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-69-8","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":69,"verse":8,"english":"Having been seated, both the heroic brothers of immeasurable splendour addressed that foremost of counsellors, Sudáman, saying, 'Go, foremost of counsellors, and speedily bring over the irrepressible Ikşvāku of immeasurable splendour along with his sons and ministers.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.218,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-70-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1069008","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e836e374fc