:"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-70-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1069011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ab39ed36a59cdc0e770cfbe436cd9a193cbc864ef78632734e1b5e782ec3dfc0","compact":"bd51d526a422c0f7b5c24da11a02d3c94a0d6636113226acdf12952702d7d51c","nasal":"bd51d526a422c0f7b5c24da11a02d3c94a0d6636113226acdf12952702d7d51c"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-69-12","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":69,"verse":12,"english":"Hearing the words of that best of counsellors, the king accompanied by the saints and his adherents, came to Janaka.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-70-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1069012","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"03a112214c358c38d0d2420aa6afb9175be1c1333bf26c70b3768316218e9589","compact":"b6b504179015f30e4337485c1a9f73a2e94aabfdb65019197779825f6054658d","nasal":"10c09a4633865973ed2e55cf761e0c007998a6d57481ced6c579e6e4e3ae6109"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-69-13","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":69,"verse":13,"english":"And in company with his counsellors with his counsellors and priests and adherents, the king, foremost of those skilled in speech, spoke to Vaideha.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.926,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-70-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1069013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d1394803911080f74f4c6ddb90f2f1d533f68f2527aec35c63c8cdeb0f1421f6","compact":"45fb40a8aea7b370a0663bc5e5e00de1e35cd40aa322667d0ee36c1bdf9a9682","nasal":"17e8640c4ec799852d05c505bf35f461626d39f7780506dde59416c79a43e8be"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-69-14","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":69,"verse":14,"english":"O mighty king, you know that the worshipful saint Vasiştha is the spiritual guide of our race; and in every ceremony that we undertake, he it is who serves the function of a spokesman.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-70-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1069014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"41c0c2394cac3777ff34663eca838ca7fa65e1c44711c09a80ebc7a852244556","compact":"e27e856509cd4351f12a4269e66d81aa7e3bc29ba07adcc8efecde45c15b985e","nasal":"e27e856509cd4351f12a4269e66d81aa7e3bc29ba07adcc8efecde45c15b985e"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-69-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":69,"verse":15,"english":"And permitted by Viśvāmitra along with all the Maharsis, even this one of a righteous soul will relate my genealogy.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.901,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-70-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1069015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a1a14073b97266a3ee2890aff97acdab03b251d4b58b962f594728d4535cf1b4","compact":"341b32c2e44d8a8a2805da9bb9f4fa9fdf60c46a15e798da262239cc7e834d20","nasal":"341b32c2e44d8a8a2805da9bb9f4fa9fdf60c46a15e798da262239cc7e834d20"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-69-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":69,"verse":16,"english":"And on Dasaratha resuming silence, the worshipful saint Vasistha, versed in speech, spoke to Vaideha in company with his priests, saying,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-70-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1069016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e294c7effe82b8eb75f79f2c84cf01d23e63d016d6e3eacd69027b103d0414fd","compact":"a0ab53d66b1951d26ade295934dc053b5c2bff281ac40dc78034961a6fb5dea5","nasal":"a0ab53d66b1951d26ade295934dc053b5c2bff281ac40dc78034961a6fb5dea5"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-69-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":69,"verse":17,"english":"The perpetual, everlasting, and undeteriorating Brahmā sprang from the Unmanifest (Brahmā). From him sprang Marīci; and Kasyapa is son to Marīci. And from Kaśyapa sprung Vivasvat; and Manu is son to Vivasvat.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-70-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1069017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eb8df16a90aef3b7c38159ebf680a49d279749f0280b27bf0b88d8978d23d6bd","compact":"159d25d0ca5b4842eeb4df1355192b5537ebcd41197c01bb43c918059e8d3a71","nasal":"159d25d0ca5b4842eeb4df1355192b5537ebcd41197c01bb43c918059e8d3a71"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-69-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":69,"verse":18,"english":"The perpetual, everlasting, and undeteriorating Brahmā sprang from the Unmanifest (Brahmā). From him sprang Marīci; and Kasyapa is son to Marīci. And from Kaśyapa sprung Vivasvat; and Manu is son to Vivasvat. This Manu is otherwise called Prajäpati; and Ikşvāku is Manu's son. And this Ikşvāku you must understand, was the first king of Ayodhyā.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.36,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-70-17","DUTT-1-70-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1069018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b80e750297f206f1d7f1324e1ffb6bde8218af14a465107f5c9fb4892a07c592","compact":"726707de0945c1f9b2adf1a4962ebd1831616703c21c422efcee175d3234c37c","nasal":"726707de0945c1f9b2adf1a4962ebd1831616703c21c422efcee175d3234c37c"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-69-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":69,"verse":19,"english":"This Manu is otherwise called Prajäpati; and Ikşvāku is Manu's son. And this Ikşvāku you must understand, was the first king of Ayodhyā. And Ikşvāku's son, it is well known, was the graceful Kuksi. And Kuksi's son was the graceful Vikuksi.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.493,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-70-18","DUTT-1-70-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1069019","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7889fa68246bbd5b168b49f6e9103069cfa0cacac8895c38bfa90656245cf9b3","compact":"35d1339bb65253e587eb8a84c507af1062e571449c46ed3fe411ac46b17b2ab5","nasal":"35d1339bb65253e587eb8a84c507af1062e571449c46ed3fe411ac46b17b2ab5"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-69-20","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":69,"verse":20,"english":"And Vikuksi's son was the exceedingly energetic and powerful Bāņa. And Bāna's son was the highly energetic and powerful Anaranya.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-70-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1069020","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7541592bc61999aa6c3028432cc5d9166487cfddc5f28a739398e05bd6ae8907","compact":"2bb05c195955fd40cb6276938890d51a77cd1359ca08edcab5b11e47158f4868","nasal":"2bb05c195955fd40cb6276938890d51a77cd1359ca08edcab5b11e47158f4868"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-69-21","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":69,"verse":21,"english":"From Anaranya sprang Prithu; and from Prithu, Trisanku. And Trisanku's son was the highly famous Dhundhumāra.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-70-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1069021","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"08825742c9c0c9b3fe771ffe03d970ff6660ca4e82a192e239eec9e4d3739285","compact":"2cb3f8bbdfd1e72a28c38bc16201062b3b5834d1966fa4971351b62b8faed73a","nasal":"4377832c4df130a0b2f26867dbfb07644aee8a2b32eed96d3c4bbfea7167aeac"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-69-22","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":69,"verse":22,"english":"And from Dhundhumāra 